{"question_id": "505af2f5", "type": "single-session-preference", "label": true, "judge": "Yes.", "question": "I was thinking of trying a new coffee creamer recipe. Any recommendations?", "gold": "The user would prefer responses that suggest variations on their existing almond milk, vanilla extract, and honey creamer recipe or new ideas that align with their goals of reducing sugar intake and saving money. They might not prefer responses that recommend commercial creamer products or recipes that are high in sugar or expensive.", "hypothesis": "Since you've been making your own flavored creamer with almond milk, vanilla extract, and honey, here\u2019s a new recipe you might enjoy:\n\n**Coconut Vanilla Creamer**\n\n*Ingredients:*\n- 1 cup unsweetened almond milk (or coconut milk for a richer flavor)\n- 1/2 cup canned coconut milk\n- 1-2 tablespoons vanilla extract (adjust to taste)\n- 1-2 tablespoons honey or a low-carb sweetener (like stevia or monk fruit)\n- A pinch of salt\n\n*Instructions:*\n1. In a mixing bowl, combine the almond milk and coconut milk.\n2. Add the vanilla extract and honey (or sweetener) and whisk until well combined.\n3. Add a pinch of salt to enhance the flavors.\n4. Pour the mixture into an airtight container and store it in the refrigerator for up to a week.\n5. Shake well before each use, as the ingredients may separate.\n\nThis coconut vanilla creamer will add a delicious tropical twist to your coffee while keeping it creamy and flavorful. Enjoy experimenting with this new recipe!", "judge_model": "openai/gpt-4o-2024-08-06", "provider": "OpenAI"}
